                "tuning.coil.intro": "On a traditional coil machine, the voltage readout is only one part of the circuit. Contact screw gap, front and rear spring tension, armature bar weight, and capacitor microfarad rating (uF) dictate the stroke cycle.",
                "tuning.coil.order.title": "Proper Mechanical Tuning Order for Coils:",
                "tuning.coil.order.1": "1. Mechanical alignment: Seat needle bar, grommet, and tube straight without lateral binding.",
                "tuning.coil.order.2": "2. Contact screw gap: Adjust screw gap (dime-thickness for liner, nickel-thickness for shader as a physical baseline).",
                "tuning.coil.order.3": "3. Spring tension: Adjust rear spring angle to balance armature return speed before raising voltage.",
                "tuning.coil.order.4": "4. Fine voltage calibration: Adjust power supply voltage only after mechanics and springs are aligned.",
                "tuning.coil.limits.title": "What Voltage CAN and CANNOT Fix on a Coil:",
